                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69f98ffb-255c-3f4a-b496-8b0f9c6bd6a3",
                        "entry_id": "27a99762-89c4-3a8d-898c-15eccdacf74d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A low-pitched beeping sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "910c9c0e-3166-45d4-8cc9-094b028d5510",
                                "sense_id": "69f98ffb-255c-3f4a-b496-8b0f9c6bd6a3",
                                "text": "When something important happened, a polite sort of boop went off, and up in the right-hand corner of your screen, above the copy, a word or two appeared: Urgent, Bulletin, Late Stocks, whatever."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43065199-f0e4-4280-80d3-e2083882e057",
                                "sense_id": "69f98ffb-255c-3f4a-b496-8b0f9c6bd6a3",
                                "text": "Originally, computers' attempts at making music were recognizable by their beeps and boops and weird swoops. And to suggest that the rhythms laid down by a^([sic]) electronic drummer were anything close to swingin' was humorous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1963f4b-2bdc-478b-bdbd-126b8f806229",
                                "sense_id": "69f98ffb-255c-3f4a-b496-8b0f9c6bd6a3",
                                "text": "Guitars riffle precise chords and lilt through arpeggios, keyboards go boop, and every flick of a drumbeat is in place."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "015522f8-f9ec-476e-a403-d6023b736c69",
                                "sense_id": "69f98ffb-255c-3f4a-b496-8b0f9c6bd6a3",
                                "text": "Santogold, from Brooklyn, may be mocking scene pretensions, defending the creative impulse or both in her single, “L.E.S. Artistes,” with its drumstick-clicking beat, electro boops and dance-rock chorus."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c6e8c28-dfde-35c9-bdb0-35e60d0eacb6",
                        "entry_id": "27a99762-89c4-3a8d-898c-15eccdacf74d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A gentle or playful tap or strike, especially on the nose."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e94ee1b1-0ca4-4dd8-a4e5-25bf00c5de8a",
                                "sense_id": "5c6e8c28-dfde-35c9-bdb0-35e60d0eacb6",
                                "text": "“Boop, on the nose! Boop, on the nose! Boop, on the nose!” “He's bypassing our shields. We can't take many more boops.” “Thanks to Father giving me full access to Starfleet data systems, I know all possible shield frequencies. Boop!”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
